From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:23:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 145/151] Find: Replace selects the match first and replaces it
 on the next press, as in Notepad++

Notepad++ replaces only when the selection is the match there: a first
press on a fresh query selects the next match, the next press replaces
it and selects the one after. Replace, Replace across lines and Replace
inside "In selection" now work that way. An empty selection at an empty
match (`^` at the cursor) counts as selected, so `^` replaces at once.
After a replace the next match is selected, skipping only an empty
match right at the replacement's end (as Replace all does).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

